        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Valparaiso University, Old Dominion University, College of William & Mary\n- Places: Norfolk, Virginia, United States, Hampton Roads\n- Concepts: university type, enrollment, campus size, founding\n\nFacts:\n- Old Dominion University was established in 1930 as the Norfolk Division of the College of William & Mary.\n- For the 2014-2015 academic year, Old Dominion University enrolled 24,670 students and was one of the largest universities in Virginia.\n- Old Dominion University is a public, co-educational research university in Norfolk, Virginia, United States, with two satellite campuses in the Hampton Roads area.\n- Valparaiso University, commonly known as Valpo, is a coeducational four-year Lutheran institution.\n- Valparaiso University enrolls about 4,500 students from over 50 countries on a 350-acre campus.",
